{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "label": "FSM<SName, SData, Message>", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "In-Memory-Zustandsmaschine, DSL-getrieben. Uebergaenge werden im Subklassen-Konstruktor konfiguriert; das onReceive der Basisklasse routet jede Message zum Handler des aktuellen Zustands.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_when", "label": "when(state, handler)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Der Handler bekommt aktuelle Zustands-Daten und eingehende Message und gibt einen Transition zurueck. Async-Handler serialisieren wie jedes Actor.onReceive - ein Timer-Tick waehrend des Awaits wartet auf den Handler.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_goto", "label": "goto(state, data)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Uebergang: feuert onExitState fuer den aktuellen Zustand, setzt neuen Zustand + Daten, feuert onEnter fuer den neuen Zustand.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_stay", "label": "stay(data)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Kein Uebergang, aber Daten werden aktualisiert; weder onEnter noch onExitState feuern. Fuer unbehandelte Messages explizit stay(data) zurueckgeben.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_onenter", "label": "onEnter(state, hook)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Natuerliche Heimat fuer Timer-Setup beim Zustandseintritt. In diesen Callbacks geworfene Fehler werden abgefangen und als Warnung geloggt - sie erreichen den Supervisor nicht, und der Uebergang wird trotzdem abgeschlossen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_onexitstate", "label": "onExitState(state, hook)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Gegenstueck zu onEnter - der Ort, an dem in onEnter aufgesetzte Timer wieder abgebaut werden.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_ontransition", "label": "onTransition(listener)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Feuert bei jedem Uebergang mit From-State, To-State und neuen Daten - fuer globale Instrumentierung, ohne Per-State-Callbacks aufzulisten. Mehrere Listener werden unterstuetzt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_restart_semantics", "label": "FSM-Restart-Semantik", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Beim Neustart laeuft der Konstruktor erneut und die FSM beginnt beim initialen Zustand + Daten. Kein Event-Log zum Abspielen - wenn der State Neustarts ueberleben muss, ist PersistentFSM das Werkzeug.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_immutable_state_data", "label": "State-Daten immutable und serialisierbar halten", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Pro Transition wird ein neues Objekt produziert; Mutationen funktionieren technisch, brechen aber Testbarkeit und Reasoning. Keine Closures und keine Actor-Refs in State-Daten - sie ueberleben keinen Neustart, koennen leaken und blockieren die spaetere Migration zu PersistentFSM.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_when", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_goto", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_stay", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_goto", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_onenter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_goto", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_onexitstate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_ontransition", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_restart_semantics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_fsm", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_immutable_state_data", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_stay", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_restart_semantics", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_persistent_fsm_persistentfsm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_fsm_fsm_immutable_state_data", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_durable_state_immutable_state", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/fsm/fsm.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}